The full documentation can be found at https://docs.phoenix-rtos.com.

This repository contains all the necessary files needed to build
Phoenix-RTOS Documentation using sphinx.

Here are few steps to prepare environment:
- sudo apt update
- sudo apt install latexmk texlive-xetex texlive-latex-extra
- sudo apt install fonts-liberation fonts-dejavu fonts-noto-core fonts-freefont-ttf
- sudo apt install texlive-lang-polish (only for documents built in Polish)
- sudo apt install python3-pip
- sudo apt install python3-venv
- ./prepare_venv.py
- source _venv/bin/activate

The fonts are the ones the documents are typeset with, so an environment that
has none of them, a bare container among them, needs them as well: Liberation
Sans for the text, DejaVu Sans Mono for the code blocks, and Noto Sans Symbols2
with FreeSans for the icons.

To build html or pdf versions:
- make html
- make latexpdf

The output files will be available in _build directory.

Optionally run make clean to clear _build directory.

The language of the generated documents is set by the 'language' option in
conf.py ("en" or "pl"). It can be also overridden for a single build, then
a separate build directory is worth using to keep both variants:
- make latexpdf BUILDDIR=_build/pl O="-D language=pl"

